course: dictionary
lesson: 2113
title: How heat moves by convection
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heat can travel in three ways, and convection is one of them. Convection happens in liquids and gases, like water and air. «Convection carries heat with moving air or water: warm air rises and cool air sinks.»
explain: Here is how it works. When part of a liquid or gas is heated, it becomes lighter and rises. The cooler part is heavier, so it sinks to take its place. This movement makes a loop called a convection current that goes round and round.
explain: You can see convection in everyday things. A radiator warms a room because warm air rises from it and cooler air sinks down to be heated. Wind and sea currents form in the same way. Look for the clue words "rises" and "sinks": they show the heat is moving with the flow.
fact: Convection is one of three ways heat travels: conduction, convection and radiation.
fact: Convection happens in liquids and gases, such as water and air.
fact: A «convection current» is a loop of moving water or air that carries heat round.
fact: A «convection oven» uses a fan to move hot air around the food.
fact: Convection does not work in a solid, such as a metal spoon. There, heat moves by conduction.
exercise: «Convection carries heat with moving air or water.» What carries the heat in convection? | A solid metal spoon | Empty space | *Moving air or water | Sunlight only
exercise: In convection, what does warm air do? | Stays still in one place | Sinks to the floor | *Rises | Turns into ice
exercise: Which of these is a use of convection? | Cutting bread with a knife | Fixing a bike chain | *Warming a room from a radiator | Lighting a torch with a battery
test: Why does the cooler air sink in a room? | It is hotter than the warm air above it | It has been pushed out of the window | It wants to go to sleep | *It is heavier than the warm air above it
test: What is a «convection current»? | *A loop of moving water or air that carries heat round | A solid lump of metal that gets hot | A sound that travels through a wall | A beam of light from the sun
exam: Which sentence describes convection correctly? | Convection only happens in space | Heat moves through a solid spoon by convection | Cool air rises and warm air sinks | *Warm air rises and cool air sinks, making a current that goes round
